{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgyg8r1wkb","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Verify a live embedding rollout by counting note_vecs_set events, not the reembed embedded total; restart the daemon AFTER the merge","summary":"Two operational gotchas hit during the Phase-1 note.vecs rollout. (1) The /overlay/reembed and /overlay/backfill-embeddings 'embedded' count is MISLEADING for multivec: field .vecs and the note_vecs_set event are written only inside if(vecs.length) at routes/overlay.js:648, but 'embedded' increments on the POOLED .vec re-embed and failed field embeds are silently dropped by .filter(Boolean). So a run can report embedded=502, failed=0 while writing ZERO .vecs. To verify a multivec backfill actually took, count real events: grep '\\\"evt\\\":\\\"note_vecs_set\\\"' over .graph/nodes (the plain string also appears as text inside note summaries, so match the event key). (2) A daemon restarted BEFORE a feature->main merge runs stale pre-merge code. The first backfill produced 0 .vecs because the live daemon had started at 13:15 — four minutes before the merge commit at 13:19 — so it ran the old reembed handler. Detect a stale daemon by comparing its process StartTime to the merge commit time (git log -1 --format=%cd --date=local <sha>); the daemon StartTime must be AFTER the merge. After the post-merge daemon (pid 28520, 13:57) came up, re-running /overlay/reembed force:true populated .vecs on all 502 active notes (502 note_vecs_set events; 811 total note files incl. superseded). The field-embed code is correct: noteFieldTexts returns [title, summary, ...per-knowledge texts] and both sequential and concurrent (Promise.all) embeds succeed.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T18:07:54.445Z","vec":[-0.08469801396131516,-0.04789786413311958,-0.02175586111843586,-0.007583362050354481,0.06680505722761154,-0.029404999688267708,-0.07145404070615768,0.055674679577350616,0.06690099835395813,0.004264673683792353,0.04732990264892578,0.012240324169397354